## Title: Under Pressure
## Author: Th3rtythr33
## Version: 0.2.8
## AddOnVersion: 9
## APIVersion: 101049 101050
## SavedVariables: UnderPressureSavedVars
## DependsOn: LibAddonMenu-2.0>=32
## Description: Quickly see how much danger you are in and how long you have to live if the damage isn't healed through or mitigated. Also provides a counter of how many distinct mobs you are taking damage from, with a Tank Mode to provide a count of what mobs you may not have under your control.

; AddOnVersion tracks the LAST PUBLISHED build, which is 0.2.7 = 8. It must
; only ever increase. This was briefly set to 30 while the release was
; planned as 3.0; that build was never published, so stepping back to 9 is
; safe here and would NOT be safe if 30 had ever shipped.
;
; DependsOn (not Optional) is correct: LibAddonMenu-2.0 IS listed on the
; Bethesda.net console portal, confirmed by the author 2026-07-28, so the
; dependency resolves and gets auto-installed there. Do not "fix" this to
; OptionalDependsOn -- that was tried in 0.2.8 development on the mistaken
; belief that LAM was unavailable on console, and it would cost users the
; auto-install and therefore the settings panel entirely.
;
; The Description directive above must stay a SINGLE line (manifest
; directives cannot wrap) and should match the Bethesda.net listing copy.
; Note the two render differently: the Bethesda.net web listing takes a
; markdown-like syntax, while the IN-GAME add-on browser uses ESO's own
; |cRRGGBB|r colour codes. Plain text like this is the safe intersection.

; Load order: bootstrap -> engine -> UI -> settings -> main entry
; Fonts.lua must load before any UI that sets a font.

Engine/FeatureDetect.lua
Engine/AbilityClassifier.lua
Engine/AttackerTracker.lua
Engine/PressureEngine.lua
Engine/EventIngest.lua

UI/Fonts.lua
UI/Indicator.xml
UI/Indicator.lua
UI/Debug.xml
UI/Debug.lua

Settings.lua

UnderPressure.lua
